144:- DOS-8 inline UI uses the typed enum directly. No more untyped `feedback_yes/no/wrong_source` handlers.
146:### 6. Subject correction interplay (ADR-0105 amendment)
148:`WrongSubject { corrected_to }` is the user-side complement to ADR-0105's `SubjectAttribution` substrate primitive. Behavior:
150:- `corrected_to: None` — "this content does not belong to this entity; I don't know whose it is." Tombstone the claim at the asserted subject only; do not propose a new attachment.
151:- `corrected_to: Some(SubjectRef)` — "this content belongs to that entity instead." Tombstone at the asserted subject; propose (not commit) a new claim at the corrected subject with the same claim_text, full provenance preserved, `actor = 'user_correction'`. The corrected claim enters via the standard propose/commit path so it gets the same gate as any other claim.
153:The inference method that produced the wrong attachment receives `subject_evidence` downweight `-0.3`. After repeated `WrongSubject` feedback against the same `InferenceMethod` for the same source class, the inference method gets globally suppressed for that source class (threshold: 5 instances within 30 days).
159:1. A `claim_repair_job` row is enqueued via DOS-236 invalidation queue with `priority = normal`.
163:5. No corroboration within 14 days → claim downweights via `lack-of-corroboration` factor; lint surface flags it.
165:Budgets: 1 LLM call + 1 retrieval batch per job; max 5 active repair jobs per entity; max 50 per workspace. Excess queues at `priority = low`.
169:- UI surfaces beyond DOS-8's inline six. Overflow menu (`NeedsNuance` editor, `SurfaceInappropriate`, `NotRelevantHere`), claim detail panel, lint feedback debt — v1.4.2.
170:- Cross-claim feedback aggregation ("user often marks Glean Salesforce sources wrong" → systematic source downweight). Tracked separately for v1.5.0+.
171:- Feedback from non-User actors. Enum supports `created_by: ClaimActor` for future agent-to-agent feedback; v1.4.0 commits user-only.
179:- Trust Compiler's `user_feedback_weight` factor has a typed input, not a placeholder.
182:- `CannotVerify` does not punish claims for user uncertainty — closes the feedback-as-noise risk that yes/no would have introduced.
190:- Repair job queue depends on DOS-236 (durable invalidation), which is v1.4.1 scope. v1.4.0 ships the `claim_repair_job` row schema + enqueue stub; the worker runs in v1.4.1. `CannotVerify` feedback collected in v1.4.0 is queued and processed once the worker lands.
