.docs/decisions/0125-claim-anatomy-temporal-sensitivity-typeregistry.md:11:The 2026-04-24 Claim Anatomy Review (`.docs/plans/claim-anatomy-review-2026-04-24.md`) walked every dimension a claim should express in the v1.4.x substrate. Three dimensions were under-scrutinized at the substrate level and warrant a substrate primitive in v1.4.0 spine:
.docs/decisions/0125-claim-anatomy-temporal-sensitivity-typeregistry.md:13:1. **Temporal scope** (Review §11) — distinguishes PointInTime / State / Trend claims; affects freshness, supersession, and contradiction semantics.
.docs/decisions/0125-claim-anatomy-temporal-sensitivity-typeregistry.md:14:2. **Sensitivity** (Review §12) — claim-level sensitivity tier; structural safeguard against accidental surface leakage.
