.docs/decisions/0124-longitudinal-topic-threading.md:6:**Extends:** [ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) (SubjectAttribution amendment), [ADR-0113](0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md) (claims)
.docs/decisions/0124-longitudinal-topic-threading.md:11:DailyOS today produces strong cross-thread synthesis on **current** signals — recognizing that two concurrent renewal cycles + cross-portfolio role + recent pipeline-risk signal compose into a leverage-relevant moment, for example. It does not retrieve **the longitudinal narrative thread** the user has been building over many prior sessions on the same theme — months of 1:1 reasoning about consolidation strategy that gives the moment its weight.
.docs/decisions/0124-longitudinal-topic-threading.md:15:- Per-`(entity_id, claim_type, field_path)` claim history ([ADR-0113](0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md) R1.6).
.docs/decisions/0124-longitudinal-topic-threading.md:16:- Multi-subject claims spanning Account / Project / Person / Meeting ([ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) SubjectAttribution amendment).
.docs/decisions/0124-longitudinal-topic-threading.md:19:None of these models a **longitudinal topic / theme / initiative** — a thread the user has been actively working over time that spans entities and accumulates reasoning across many sessions. Without one, surfaces miss the historical weight that makes a current signal meaningful.
.docs/decisions/0124-longitudinal-topic-threading.md:34:ALTER TABLE intelligence_claims ADD COLUMN thread_id TEXT NULL;
