.docs/plans/wave-W1/DOS-311-plan.md:50:3. **Worker drain protocol** — a way to tell `intel_queue` (and any other workers) to finish in-flight work and pause new dequeues during a migration. DOS-7's migration runs the 7-step sequence: pre-flight log → bump epoch → drain workers → backfill → requeue → reconcile → re-enable.
