.docs/plans/wave-W1/DOS-311-plan.md:242:- `concurrent_writer_during_drain_rejected` — a worker writes during the drain phase; assert FenceError::EpochAdvanced.
.docs/plans/wave-W1/DOS-311-plan.md:252:- **Epoch table separate from `entity_graph_version` and `global_claim_epoch`**: three different invalidation domains. `entity_graph_version` is entity-linking (DOS-258). `global_claim_epoch` is Global-subject claims (DOS-310). `schema_epoch` is structural-migration cutover (DOS-311). Sharing counters would re-introduce the singleton-counter thrash (Codex round-1 finding 4).
.docs/plans/wave-W1/DOS-311-plan.md:254:- **DOS-311 PR1 does NOT migrate existing callers** to the fence. Allowlist transitions them in W3 alongside DOS-7's 9-mechanism consolidation. PR1 ships the fence + drain + reconcile + 3 fixtures.
.docs/plans/wave-W1/DOS-311-plan.md:265:- **Migration audit trail**: `schema_epoch.bumped_at` + `bumped_by` fields capture who bumped the epoch (v1.4.0: `system`; v1.5+: optional user identifier for manual ops). Cycle-1 reviewer confirms.
.docs/plans/wave-W1/DOS-311-plan.md:267:- **Worker drain race**: a malicious caller can't trigger the fence-rejection path because epoch bumps require a privileged migration call (`db.bump_schema_epoch(...)` with a guard).
.docs/plans/wave-W1/DOS-311-plan.md:272:- **Per-write fence overhead**: 1 SELECT on `schema_epoch` (single-row indexed lookup) — ~10-50µs on SQLite. Negligible vs. the file write itself (~1ms+).
.docs/plans/wave-W1/DOS-311-plan.md:277:- **Migration-time cost**: drain is bounded by in-flight enrichment latency (~30s worst case for a Glean-fallback PTY job). Acceptable for a one-time migration.
.docs/plans/wave-W1/DOS-311-plan.md:281:- **Services-only mutations**: schema_epoch writes flow through `db.bump_schema_epoch(...)` (new helper); CI lint enforces. Direct UPDATE rejected.
.docs/plans/wave-W1/DOS-311-plan.md:297:- **DOS-310 (W1-A)** owns: per-entity claim_version columns, `db/claim_invalidation.rs`, sorted-lock helper. **No file overlap** with this PR.
.docs/plans/wave-W1/DOS-311-plan.md:300:  - **DOS-7 (W3-C, post-2026-04-26 absorbing DOS-308)**: executes the 7-step migration sequence using this PR's primitives. DOS-7's migration consumes `bump_schema_epoch` + `intel_queue.pause()/drain()/resume()` + the reconcile fixtures.
.docs/plans/wave-W1/DOS-311-plan.md:307:- **Migration safety**: `schema_epoch` table is additive. Existing queries are unaffected (no joins against it). Default value 0 means existing fence-cycle reads succeed against a fresh DB.
.docs/plans/wave-W1/DOS-311-plan.md:308:- **Drain timeout**: if drain doesn't complete within a reasonable window (e.g., 60s), the migration aborts with a hard error. Operators retry. Cycle-1 reviewer: confirm timeout mechanism is in scope vs. deferred to DOS-7.
.docs/plans/wave-W1/DOS-311-plan.md:309:- **Concurrent writes during drain**: rejected by the fence (epoch advanced). The caller logs FenceError::EpochAdvanced; DOS-301's projection sweep repaints the entity on next claim touch.
.docs/plans/wave-W1/DOS-311-plan.md:312:- **Rollback path**: revert the migration drops the `schema_epoch` table (SQLite ≥3.35) or leaves it as a no-op (older SQLite). Either way, no data corruption — the table is additive.
