     2	--
     3	-- WHEN THIS RUNS: at step 6 of DOS-7's 7-step migration sequence (pre-flight
     4	-- log → bump epoch → drain → backfill → requeue → reconcile → resume), AFTER
     5	-- DOS-7's 9-mechanism consolidation has populated `intelligence_claims`.
     6	--
     7	-- DEFINITION OF GHOST RESURRECTION: an active item present in any legacy
     8	-- projection (`entity_intelligence` JSON columns, `intelligence.json` file
     9	-- content, `accounts.company_overview`/`strategic_programs`/`notes`) that
    10	-- matches a tombstoned claim by `(subject_ref, claim_type, field_path,
    11	-- dedup_key OR item_hash)` AND has no newer `source_asof` than the
    12	-- tombstone's `dismissed_at`.
    13	--
    14	-- ZERO findings = clean migration. Any findings = stale projection that
    15	-- DOS-301's projection sweep (W3-D) or this script's `--repair` mode
    16	-- consumes.
    17	--
    18	-- CROSS-ISSUE NOTE (DOS-311 W1 ship-time): this SQL references
    19	-- `intelligence_claims` which DOES NOT YET EXIST in the W1 codebase.
    20	-- DOS-7 (W3-C) ships the table; the SQL below is committed as a static
    21	-- asset that DOS-7's migration script consumes via include_str! when the
    22	-- table is in place. Until DOS-7 lands, this SQL is documentation /
    23	-- contract only.
    24	--
    25	-- The view `legacy_projection_state` is also a DOS-7 deliverable: it
    26	-- materializes a unified shape over `entity_intelligence` JSON columns,
    27	-- `intelligence.json` file content, and account narrative columns. Its
    28	-- columns must include `(subject_ref, claim_type, field_path, dedup_key,
    29	-- sourced_at, projection_target)`.
    30	
    31	-- Match-key contract: a projected item resurrects a tombstoned claim when
    32	-- ANY of the following hold (inclusive OR), in addition to the
    33	-- (subject_ref, claim_type, field_path) triple agreeing:
    34	--   1. dedup_key match (canonicalized item key)
    35	--   2. item_hash match (content fingerprint; survives dedup_key changes)
    36	--
    37	-- The item_hash fallback catches items whose dedup_key shifted post-tombstone
    38	-- (e.g., a re-enrichment regenerated the canonical key) but whose content
    39	-- fingerprint still matches the dismissed item. Live ticket DOS-311 calls
    40	-- this out explicitly: "(dedup_key OR item_hash)".
    41	
    42	WITH tombstoned_claims AS (
    43	    SELECT
    44	        subject_ref,
    45	        claim_type,
    46	        field_path,
    47	        dedup_key,
    48	        item_hash,
    49	        source_asof,
    50	        created_at AS dismissed_at
    51	    FROM intelligence_claims
    52	    WHERE claim_state = 'tombstoned'
    53	      AND superseded_at IS NULL
    54	)
    55	SELECT
    56	    pi.subject_ref,
    57	    pi.claim_type,
